{"name":"Vanity","hex":"#5692b2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vanity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vanity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vanity","blocks":[{"text":"Vanity is the excessive belief in one's own abilities or attractiveness. Prior to the 14th century, it did not have such narcissistic undertones, and merely meant futility. The related term vainglory is now often seen as an archaic synonym for vanity, but originally meant considering one's own capabilities and that God's help was not needed, i.e. unjustified boasting; although glory is now seen as having a predominantly positive meaning, the Latin term from which it derives, gloria, roughly means boasting, and was often used as a negative criticism."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanity","wikidata":"Q1321250"},{"title":"Vanity (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Denise Katherine Matthews, known professionally as Vanity, was a Canadian singer, songwriter, dancer, model, and actress. Known for her image as a sex symbol in the 1980s, in the 1990s she renounced her career as Vanity and became an evangelist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Denise_%22Vanity%22_Matthews.jpg/330px-Denise_%22Vanity%22_Matthews.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanity_(singer)","wikidata":"Q715175"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Perrault_Leon_Jean_Basile_Vanitas.jpg/960px-Perrault_Leon_Jean_Basile_Vanitas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Perrault_Leon_Jean_Basile_Vanitas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Perrault_Leon_Jean_Basile_Vanitas.jpg/960p